{
 "name": "hibbertopterus",
 "description": "Hibbertopterus, the giant Carboniferous sweep-feeding sea scorpion (about 1.6 m long, 1 m wide), top 3/4 view walking right: very broad, rounded, flattened head shield much wider than long with a visible dark lower rim, two small close-set eyes, wide armoured body of nine plates (pointed side corners, dark side wall) tapering to a short pointed tail, two pairs of long spiny raking blades held forward, two pairs of sturdy walking legs. Mud brown #6f5a3e with spray texture. Not jaekelopterus: no pincers, no paddles, no long spike. Anchor centre, ~670x440 (x -334..338, y -224..224).",
